  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "ZAQ_head": "Please read each statement carefully and indicate how much you agree or disagree.",
      "ZAQ_r1": "Strongly disagree",
      "ZAQ_r2": "Disagree",
      "ZAQ_r3": "Agree",
      "ZAQ_r4": "Strongly agree",
      "ZAQ001": "I prefer not to break the law, no matter how minor.",
      "ZAQ002": "I dislike when other people touch me when we are talking (for example if they lay a hand on my shoulder).",
      "ZAQ003": "I sometimes have the feeling that I am watching myself from outside my body.",
      "ZAQ004": "I have sometimes felt that other people were able to read my mind.",
      "ZAQ005": "It is difficult for me to understand social \"rules\" e.g., at family gatherings or with a group of friends. Therefore, I either don't go at all or I get very anxious before going.",
      "ZAQ006": "Negotiating is difficult for me in many situations e.g., prices at flea markets, buying/selling used cars, clothes or electronics, or negotiating salary in a job interview.",
      "ZAQ007": "I can easily tell if someone else is interested or bored with what I am saying and I easily adjust to this.",
      "ZAQ008": "I usually see patterns in many things that other people don't notice.",
      "ZAQ009": "I find it easy to point out a friend in the crowd.",
      "ZAQ010": "I always want to be seated in the same spot.",
      "ZAQ011": "When I am at home during the day, I keep the shades or curtains down, because I am bothered by the light.",
      "ZAQ012": "Sometimes I feel that I am not really present in this world.",
      "ZAQ013": "I believe that ghosts or spirits can influence my life.",
      "ZAQ014": "I often feel so disconnected from the world that it is difficult for me to do things.",
      "ZAQ015": "If I'm invited to a party, without knowing the specifics of it (e.g., are the plans to eat, dance or just relax? How many people will be coming? Who? What is the menu and seating arrangement?), I get anxious, and it is difficult for me to participate.",
      "ZAQ016": "When I am home alone without any plans, most of the time I am relaxed and mentally undisturbed.",
      "ZAQ017": "I can sense if I am being intrusive even if the other person doesn't tell me.",
      "ZAQ018": "I think I sometimes bore others, when I go into details about the things I talk about.",
      "ZAQ019": "It is very important, almost necessary, for me to make a shopping list before I go grocery shopping.",
      "ZAQ020": "In primary school, I had better math skills than most of my fellow students.",
      "ZAQ021": "When I am at social occasions, I find myself repeating the same topics or questions, especially if I previously have received a positive response doing so.",
      "ZAQ022": "I am sensitive to smells. E.g. I leave or move to another section when I smell a strong odour in a store (for example, bath products, candles, perfumes).",
      "ZAQ023": "Sometimes when I look in the mirror my face seems quite different from usual.",
      "ZAQ024": "I am worried that people on other planets may be influencing what happens on Earth.",
      "ZAQ025": "Sometimes I observe that my experience of time changes dramatically. That time passes much faster or slower than usual.",
      "ZAQ026": "It is difficult for me to understand what my family or acquaintances mean during conversations, and I feel misunderstood, which is why it is hard for me to be with them.",
      "ZAQ027": "I often overthink the social encounters in my life (both the ones I have had earlier in life and the upcoming), to such a degree that it makes my daily routines or my job/education difficult to carry out.",
      "ZAQ028": "As a child I struggled compared to my peers with knowing how to get along with other children.",
      "ZAQ029": "I find it difficult to write concisely: I often exceed the numbers of words allowed and find it difficult to decide which details should be left out.",
      "ZAQ030": "Earlier in my life, I have had strange (illogical) experiences, where the conception of my surroundings and my sense of self changed significantly, which made me feel insecure and stressed. As a result, I became more withdrawn and avoided being with others.",
      "ZAQ031": "I have more talent or skill than the average person within at least one of the following areas: visual art (painting, drawing), music (singing or playing), scientific experimentation, mathematics or computer science.",
      "ZAQ032": "In my teenage years, I experienced a change in myself, where I often withdrew into my own thoughts, and became occupied by them, for better or worse. I became less interested in being social and spent more time by myself.",
      "ZAQ033": "I have a tendency to think a lot about philosophical questions (like the meaning of life, or life after death) or metaphysical questions (like, are we able to understand reality, are we alone in the universe).",
      "ZAQ034": "If given a choice about what to eat, how and which route of transport to choose or what song or TV-show/film to watch, I would feel a strong urge to choose what I am used to, rather than choosing something new.",
      "ZAQ035": "Sometimes I experience unusual burning sensations or other strange feelings in or on my body, which cannot be explained by a physical illness.",
      "ZAQ036": "I have sometimes experienced that my thoughts about being alive and life are confusing. Where I often think a lot about ordinary things like: why the grass is green, why the traffic lights have three colours or why we have two eyes?",
      "ZAQ037": "Some people can make me aware of them just by thinking about me.",
      "ZAQ038": "During my adolescence, I experienced that I gradually preferred to speak less with people around me, becoming more withdrawn, with a tendency to isolate myself from others.",
      "ZAQ039": "As a child, I played with toys in an unusual way (unscrewed the wheels of a toy car but didn't play with it like a toy car or played with a doll's hair, but not the whole doll).",
      "ZAQ040": "I am more challenged than most people when trying to understand other people's perspectives.",
      "ZAQ041": "You and your friend have plans to study for an upcoming exam. Your friend arrives at your place after walking across campus in the freezing cold. You are anxious about the exam, so you immediately start reviewing the material, but your friend interrupts you saying, \"brrr it's so cold outside, I can barely feel my fingers\". What does your friend most likely mean?",
      "ZAQ042": "I often feel vulnerable and unsafe as I am unable to see threats (or opportunities) that are out of my field of vision.",
      "ZAQ043": "It is important for me to know exactly what my plans are for the upcoming days so I make detailed schedules, that I am compelled to follow.",
      "ZAQ044": "When I look at ordinary things like trees or clouds, I often search for patterns.",
      "ZAQ045": "I have sometimes experienced that my thoughts or feelings are located at a specific place in my head.",
      "ZAQ046": "In my teenage years, I experienced a change in my mood and emotions, where the positive feelings gradually became significantly toned down (downplayed).",
      "ZAQ047": "As a child/preteen I heard voices that were not based on reality (not coming from a person I could see, TV, radio etc.).",
      "ZAQ048": "I take things too literally and therefore misunderstand the actual meaning in the conversation.",
      "ZAQ049": "You just got back from a weekend trip visiting family. When you return you leave your suitcase in the common room of your apartment/dorm even though you know your roommate prefers that you keep your personal belongings in your room. Your roommate notices your suitcase and asks if you are going on another trip. What does your roommate most likely mean?",
      "ZAQ050": "I have the tendency to focus on details and patterns to a degree where I lose the overall point (for example focusing on colors or details in the background or lose the plot).",
      "ZAQ051": "When I see physical objects move around, they almost seem alive.",
      "ZAQ052": "Sometimes I have difficulty telling whether I am experiencing something or just imagining it.",
      "ZAQ053": "I have many times experienced that the sensory signals from the outside world are distorted (vague, unclear, hazy).",
      "ZAQ054": "Sometimes, I have the feeling that there is a person or force around me, even though I can't see anybody nearby.",
      "ZAQ055": "My thoughts are so hazy and unclear that I wish that I could just reach up and put them into place.",
      "ZAQ056": "During my adolescence, I gradually (from months to years) experienced a change in my mood, where I became more superficial and stopped reacting to the news with the same sadness or joy as before.",
      "ZAQ057": "As a child/preteen I had paranoid or suspicious ideas about other people's behaviour and motives.",
      "ZAQ058": "When I look at people outside from inside my house, I predominantly perceive them as physical or biological objects and less as human beings with intentions.",
      "ZAQ059": "You and your roommate usually walk to class together. You are getting ready in the bathroom when your roommate frantically runs out of the bedroom saying: \"I'm running late. Did you hear my alarm go off?\" What does your roommate most likely mean?",
      "ZAQ060": "I get preoccupied by one or more parts of objects instead of the whole object, for example buttons on clothes, wheels on cars or dimples on cheeks.",
      "ZAQ061": "Sometimes I'm unsure whether my feelings, thoughts, sensations or actions are completely my own.",
      "ZAQ062": "I have experienced that my interests changed significantly compared to earlier, so that I suddenly became very preoccupied with existential, religious, or supernatural themes.",
      "ZAQ063": "I sometimes hear my own thoughts spoken so loud in my head, that someone nearby might be able to hear them.",
      "ZAQ064": "Earlier in my life, I experienced losing control over my thoughts or my emotions, which made me feel different, insecure and confused. As a result, I had fewer social interactions and became more withdrawn.",
      "ZAQ065": "I have sometimes experienced that there is a hidden meaning, or message to me, in everything that happens around me, as if all things or events around me seem to have to do with me.",
      "ZAQ066": "I have in periods throughout my life been occupied with collecting specific items.",
      "ZAQ067": "I'm uncomfortable wearing certain fabrics (for example, wool, silk, corduroy, tags in clothing).",
      "ZAQ068": "Sometimes when I read, I feel like the words are being read by someone else.",
      "ZAQ069": "I worry that other people are out to get me.",
      "ZAQ070": "Most of the time I find it very difficult to get my thoughts in order.",
      "ZAQ071": "Earlier in my life, I experienced a permanent reduction or loss of ability to feel joy, where the world around me and life in general turned grey or felt empty.",
      "ZAQ072": "I am able to mediate diplomatically between two parties or people with a dispute. For example, between husband and wife, colleagues at work or political opponents.",
      "ZAQ073": "I find it more difficult than other people to recognize if someone means something different from what they are saying.",
      "ZAQ074": "I often focus on details when reading rather than understanding the gist.",
      "ZAQ075": "I get very distressed if plans get changed at the last minute.",
      "ZAQ076": "Even people who do not know me well, are able to sense my desires and respond to them.",
      "ZAQ077": "A bat and a ball cost $1.10 in total. The bat costs $1.00 more than the ball. How much does the ball cost?",
      "ZAQ078": "I don't have a problem with forgiving or forgetting other people's mistakes.",
      "ZAQ079": "When I hear certain sounds, voices, or music, with my eyes closed, I see colours, shapes, or letters, inside of me.",
      "ZAQ080": "Sometimes it feels like my legs, arms, or other parts of my body are not really mine.",
      "ZAQ081": "I have sometimes felt a sense of being completely unique and extraordinary in the world - as if I were the centre of the universe.",
      "ZAQ082": "I believe that I could read other peoples' minds if I really tried.",
      "ZAQ083": "Most of the time before making a decision, I thoroughly weigh the pros and cons.",
      "ZAQ084": "If it takes 5 machines 5 minutes to make 5 widgets, how long would it take 100 machines to make 100 widgets?",
      "ZAQ085": "I have periods in my life where I intensively collect information about specific things (for example car brands, bird species, types of planets, historical persons). I do this especially when I have to buy things.",
      "ZAQ086": "Sometimes when I am thinking, my thoughts seem so loud that I wonder if other people can hear them.",
      "ZAQ087": "I have sometimes felt like the world is unreal, an illusion or a deception.",
      "ZAQ088": "I have sometimes felt as if things written in magazines or things said on TV were directed towards me.",
      "ZAQ089": "I like to have the same daily routine in household chores, school or at work and I get stressed if they change.",
      "ZAQ090": "I don't like particular food textures (for example, peaches with skin, applesauce, cottage cheese).",
      "ZAQ091": "I believe that the accidents in my life are caused by mysterious forces.",
      "ZAQ092": "When I have difficulties solving a problem, I usually ask people for advice or assistance.",
      "ZAQ093": "I had more difficulty learning to read in primary school compared with other students my age.",
      "ZAQ094": "As a child, I often didn't look people directly in the eyes, except for my parents.",
      "ZAQ095": "As a child, I did not react when others wanted me to focus my attention on the same thing as them. E.g., when someone pointed at an object or a person, I did not focus on what was being pointed at.",
      "ZAQ096": "As a child, when other people smiled at me I didn't smile back.",
      "ZAQ097": "As a child or in adult life, I have had stereotypical behavior like clapping my hands, spinning around or had especially stiff and repetitive movements when excited or stressed.",
      "ZAQ098": "As a child, I liked playing with the same toy for extended periods (many hours).",
      "ZAQ099": "As a child I often bumped into people when I was walking on the streets or in a crowd.",
      "ZAQ100": "As a child I sometimes used my toys as real people. In other words, I played with my dolls and made them pour coffee and serve it or got my action figures to go out to the car and drive it.",
      "ZAQ101": "As a child I experienced vivid daydreams.",
      "ZAQ102": "As a child, I found it difficult participating in pretend play, like playing mummy and daddy, or playing cowboys and indians.",
      "ZAQ103": "As a child I believed that I had super- or magical powers.",
      "ZAQ104": "As a child I struggled compared to my peers with understanding other kids' jokes, sarcasm or deception.",
      "ZAQ105": "I have extraordinary skills (savant-like) e.g., in drawing (hyper-detailed drawings), in maths (fast mental arithmetic), in calendar calculation (the ability to provide the day of the week for any given date) and an exceptional ability to recall the details of facts or events.",
      "ZAQ106": "I would never consider riding a motorcycle without a helmet.",
      "ZAQ107": "I find it difficult to remember the story line in films, plays, or books, but I can remember specific scenes in great detail.",
      "ZAQ108": "I would without hesitation consider letting a consultant at the travel agency plan my holiday trip.",
      "ZAQ109": "When others around me turn their attention to something, I become interested in it.",
      "ZAQ110": "I believe that there are secret signs in the world if you just know how to look for them.",
      "ZAQ111": "I like being by myself with my hobbies, rather than spending time with other people.",
      "ZAQ112": "I use strategies to drown out sound (for example, close the door, cover my ears or wear ear plugs in public).",
      "ZAQ113": "In discussions it is difficult for other people to persuade me of an alternative point of view.",
      "ZAQ114": "I have sometimes had an experience that there is something magical or supernatural in the surroundings - or that we exist in a parallel universe.",
      "ZAQ115": "In a lake, there is a patch of lily pads. Every day, the patch doubles in size. If it takes 48 days for the patch to cover the entire lake, how long would it take for the patch to cover half of the lake?",
      "ZAQ116": "I have a higher reading speed than others of the same age and education level.",
      "ZAQ117": "I would not hesitate to pass off somebody else's work as my own.",
      "ZAQ118": "I dislike being in a situation where I need to make quick decisions.",
      "ZAQ119": "Every time I buy new clothes and shoes, I prefer to buy the same brands and colours.",
      "ZAQ120": "Most of the time I correct people, when they do something wrong.",
      "ZAQ121": "When I am listening to music with others (friends, family or partner), I do not get bored of listening to the same song(s) over and over again, whereas they prefer to change songs or vary the song list.",
      "ZAQ122": "I often wonder if everyone in the world is part of a secret experiment.",
      "ZAQ123": "One or both of my parents work or have an education in the field of (science/maths, engineering, IT, or none of the above).",
      "ZAQ124": "I would drive a car without wearing a seatbelt.",
      "ZAQ125": "I have more difficulty remembering addresses, phone numbers, or dates, compared with other people my age.",
      "ZAQ126": "I like to collect things and organize them by their size, colour, brand etc.",
      "ZAQ127": "I sometimes hear voices when I am alone (not coming from the radio, TV, telephone etc.).",
      "ZAQ128": "I have a hard time coming up with new ideas (for dinner, places to go with friends, vacation activities).",
      "ZAQ129": "How much time do you spend on average on social media like Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, BeReal, Snapchat etc.?",
      "ZAQ130": "How often do you smoke?"
    }
  }
}
